IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Regulations (C.R.C., c. 1246), Part II (Reconsiderations): the request for a reconsideration (29), a longer period
-- to make it (29.1), and the procedure on a reference to the Tax Court of Canada (38 to 47). Regulations 30 to 37 and 43 are repealed
-- and encoded nowhere. Interest on amounts owing (48) is in oa3-part2-interest.l4.
--
-- Part II speaks to officials: the Social Security Tribunal, the Registrar and Chief Judge of the Tax Court, a judge. Layer 1 encodes
-- what each must do, as a rule answering whether the duty has arisen on the facts given, or whom it runs to. The people who appear in
-- the procedure are not all in the keel's Party, so this module declares the ones it needs under its own label (instruction 12 of
-- KEEL-NOTES).

§ `PART II Reconsiderations`

§§ `Request for Reconsideration`

-- 29: the request is made in writing, conveyed to the Minister, and sets out (a) the name, address and Social Insurance Number or
-- Account Number of the person and (b) the grounds for the request and a statement of the facts forming its basis.
-- src:305 | 29 A request for a reconsideration under section 27.1 of the Act shall be made in writing and be conveyed to the Minister and shall set out
-- src:306 | (a) the name, address and Social Insurance Number or Account Number of the person; and
-- src:307 | (b) the grounds for the request for a reconsideration and a statement of the facts that form the basis of that request.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 29(a) (src:306)
GIVEN `the request sets out the name of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets out the address of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets out the Social Insurance Number of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets out the Account Number of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29(a): the request sets out the particulars of the person` `the request sets out the name of the person` `the request sets out the address of the person` `the request sets out the Social Insurance Number of the person` `the request sets out the Account Number of the person` MEANS
        `the request sets out the name of the person`
    AND `the request sets out the address of the person`
    AND (   `the request sets out the Social Insurance Number of the person`
         OR `the request sets out the Account Number of the person`)

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 29(b) (src:307)
GIVEN `the request sets out the grounds for the request for a reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets out a statement of the facts that form the basis of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29(b): the request sets out its grounds and the facts` `the request sets out the grounds for the request for a reconsideration` `the request sets out a statement of the facts that form the basis of the request` MEANS
        `the request sets out the grounds for the request for a reconsideration`
    AND `the request sets out a statement of the facts that form the basis of the request`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 29 (src:305)
GIVEN `the request is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is conveyed to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets out the particulars of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets out its grounds and the facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29: the request for a reconsideration under section 27.1 of the Act is made as the Regulations require` `the request is made in writing` `the request is conveyed to the Minister` `the request sets out the particulars of the person` `the request sets out its grounds and the facts` MEANS
        `the request is made in writing`
    AND `the request is conveyed to the Minister`
    AND `the request sets out the particulars of the person`
    AND `the request sets out its grounds and the facts`

-- 29.1(2)(a) and (b): the extra conditions apply to a request made after the 365-day period after the day the person is notified in
-- writing of the decision, or made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit. 365 days are counted as days, not as a year:
-- from a notice on 2020-01-01 the period ends 2020-12-31 (2020 has 366 days) and a request on 2021-01-01 is after it.
-- src:308 | 29.1 (1) For the purposes of subsection 27.1(1) and (1.1) of the Act and subject to subsection (2), the Minister may allow a longer period to make a request for reconsideration of a decision or determination if the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period and the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration.
-- src:309 | (2) The Minister must also be satisfied that the request for reconsideration has a reasonable chance of success, and that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period to make the request, if the request for reconsideration
-- src:310 | (a) is made after the 365-day period after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination; or
-- src:311 | (b) is made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit.
-- src:312 | (3) The Minister may take any necessary steps to obtain information that the Minister may require to decide whether to allow a longer period to make a request for reconsideration.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 29.1(2) (src:309-311)
GIVEN `the day on which the request for reconsideration is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination` IS A DATE
      `the person has applied again for the same benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29.1(2): the request for reconsideration is one that needs the further satisfaction of subsection (2)` `the day on which the request for reconsideration is made` `the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination` `the person has applied again for the same benefit` MEANS
        `the day on which the request for reconsideration is made` GREATER THAN (`the day that is` (`a limit in days` 365) `after` `the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination`)
    OR  `the person has applied again for the same benefit`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 29.1(1) (src:308) (src:309)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request for reconsideration is one that needs the further satisfaction of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the request for reconsideration has a reasonable chance of success` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29.1: the Minister may allow a longer period to make the request for reconsideration` `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period` `the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration` `the request for reconsideration is one that needs the further satisfaction of subsection (2)` `the Minister is satisfied that the request for reconsideration has a reasonable chance of success` `the Minister is satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period`
    AND `the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration`
    AND (   (NOT `the request for reconsideration is one that needs the further satisfaction of subsection (2)`)
         OR (    `the Minister is satisfied that the request for reconsideration has a reasonable chance of success`
             AND `the Minister is satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period`))

-- 29.1(3): the Minister may take any necessary steps to obtain the information needed to decide whether to allow a longer period. The
-- text names no condition, so the rule has no input.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 29.1(3) (src:312)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 29.1(3): the Minister may take any necessary steps to obtain information required to decide whether to allow a longer period` MEANS
    TRUE

§§ `Reference to Tax Court of Canada`

-- The people regulations 38 to 47 speak of, other than the Minister and the appellant, are officers of the Tribunal and the Court.
DECLARE `reg 38: Participant in the appeal or reference` IS ONE OF
    `reg 38: the appellant`
    `reg 38: the Minister`
    `reg 38: the Social Security Tribunal`
    `reg 38: the Registrar of the Court`
    `reg 38: the Chief Judge of the Court`
    `reg 38: the judge appointed to hear the reference`
    `reg 38: a person added as a party to the appeal`

-- 38: where a ground of appeal under 28(2) is set out in an appeal under 28(1), the Tribunal (a) notifies the appellant and the Minister
-- that the appeal on that ground has been referred to the Court and (b) transmits to the Registrar a copy of the relevant documents.
-- src:316 | 38 If a ground of appeal referred to in subsection 28(2) of the Act is set out in an appeal brought under subsection 28(1) of the Act, the Social Security Tribunal must
-- src:317 | (a) notify the appellant and the Minister that the appeal on that ground has been referred to the Court for decision under subsection 28(2) of the Act; and
-- src:318 | (b) transmit to the Registrar of the Court a copy of the documents filed in the appeal that are relevant to the ground of appeal referred to in subsection 28(2) of the Act.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 38(a) (src:316-317)
GIVEN `a ground of appeal referred to in subsection 28(2) of the Act is set out in an appeal brought under subsection 28(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 38: Participant in the appeal or reference`
`reg 38(a): the persons the Social Security Tribunal must notify that the appeal on that ground has been referred to the Court` `a ground of appeal referred to in subsection 28(2) of the Act is set out in an appeal brought under subsection 28(1) of the Act` MEANS
    IF `a ground of appeal referred to in subsection 28(2) of the Act is set out in an appeal brought under subsection 28(1) of the Act`
    THEN LIST `reg 38: the appellant`, `reg 38: the Minister`
    ELSE EMPTY

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 38(b) (src:316) (src:318)
GIVEN `a ground of appeal referred to in subsection 28(2) of the Act is set out in an appeal brought under subsection 28(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 38(b): the Social Security Tribunal must transmit to the Registrar of the Court a copy of the documents filed in the appeal that are relevant to the ground of appeal` `a ground of appeal referred to in subsection 28(2) of the Act is set out in an appeal brought under subsection 28(1) of the Act` MEANS
    `a ground of appeal referred to in subsection 28(2) of the Act is set out in an appeal brought under subsection 28(1) of the Act`

-- 38.1(1): where an appeal is made in relation to a reference and the Minister is of the opinion that a person other than the
-- appellant may be directly affected by the decision of the Court, the Minister notifies the Tribunal. (2): on notification the Tribunal
-- notifies the Registrar and the Registrar adds that person as a party. The Registrar's duty is read as following the Tribunal's notice
-- (fork F-38.1(2) in NOTES.md).
-- src:319 | 38.1 (1) Where an appeal is made in relation to a reference under subsection 28(2) of the Act and the Minister is of the opinion that a person other than the appellant may be directly affected by the decision of the Court, the Minister shall so notify the Social Security Tribunal.
-- src:320 | (2) On notification, the Social Security Tribunal shall so notify the Registrar of the Court and the Registrar shall add that person as a party to the appeal.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 38.1(1) (src:319)
GIVEN `an appeal is made in relation to a reference under subsection 28(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is of the opinion that a person other than the appellant may be directly affected by the decision of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 38.1(1): the Minister must notify the Social Security Tribunal` `an appeal is made in relation to a reference under subsection 28(2) of the Act` `the Minister is of the opinion that a person other than the appellant may be directly affected by the decision of the Court` MEANS
        `an appeal is made in relation to a reference under subsection 28(2) of the Act`
    AND `the Minister is of the opinion that a person other than the appellant may be directly affected by the decision of the Court`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 38.1(2) (src:320)
GIVEN `the Minister has notified the Social Security Tribunal under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 38.1(2): the Social Security Tribunal must notify the Registrar of the Court` `the Minister has notified the Social Security Tribunal under subsection (1)` MEANS
    `the Minister has notified the Social Security Tribunal under subsection (1)`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 38.1(2) (src:320)
GIVEN `the Social Security Tribunal has notified the Registrar of the Court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 38.1(2): the Registrar of the Court must add the person as a party to the appeal` `the Social Security Tribunal has notified the Registrar of the Court under subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the Social Security Tribunal has notified the Registrar of the Court under subsection (2)`

-- 39(1): on receiving the documents the Tribunal transmitted under 38(b), the Registrar immediately notifies the Chief Judge, the
-- Tribunal, the Minister and any person added as a party. (2): when the Chief Judge is notified, the Chief Judge appoints a judge.
-- src:321 | 39 (1) The Registrar of the Court, on receipt of the documents transmitted by the Social Security Tribunal pursuant to paragraph 38(b), shall immediately notify the Chief Judge of the Court, the Social Security Tribunal, the Minister and any person added as a party to the appeal of that receipt.
-- src:322 | (2) When the Chief Judge of the Court is notified pursuant to subsection (1), the Chief Judge shall appoint a judge of the Court to hear the reference.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 39(1) (src:321)
GIVEN `the Registrar of the Court has received the documents transmitted by the Social Security Tribunal pursuant to paragraph 38(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 38: Participant in the appeal or reference`
`reg 39(1): the persons the Registrar of the Court must immediately notify of the receipt of the documents` `the Registrar of the Court has received the documents transmitted by the Social Security Tribunal pursuant to paragraph 38(b)` `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar of the Court has received the documents transmitted by the Social Security Tribunal pursuant to paragraph 38(b)`
    THEN append (LIST `reg 38: the Chief Judge of the Court`, `reg 38: the Social Security Tribunal`, `reg 38: the Minister`) `any person added as a party`
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        `any person added as a party` MEANS
            IF `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` THEN LIST `reg 38: a person added as a party to the appeal` ELSE EMPTY

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 39(2) (src:322)
GIVEN `the Chief Judge of the Court has been notified pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 39(2): the Chief Judge of the Court must appoint a judge of the Court to hear the reference` `the Chief Judge of the Court has been notified pursuant to subsection (1)` MEANS
    `the Chief Judge of the Court has been notified pursuant to subsection (1)`

§§ `Date and Place of Reference`

-- src:325 | 40 (1) The Registrar of the Court, in consultation with the judge of the Court appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2) to hear the reference, shall fix the date, time and place for the hearing of the reference.
-- src:326 | (2) The hearing of a reference shall be held in the city, town or village in which or nearest to which the appellant is ordinarily resident unless the appellant consents in writing to the hearing being held at some other place.
-- src:327 | (3) The Registrar of the Court shall, by registered mail, notify the appellant, the Social Security Tribunal, the Minister and any person added as a party to the appeal of the date, place and time fixed for the hearing of the reference.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 40(1) (src:325)
GIVEN `a judge of the Court has been appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2) to hear the reference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40(1): the Registrar of the Court must fix the date, time and place for the hearing of the reference` `a judge of the Court has been appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2) to hear the reference` MEANS
    `a judge of the Court has been appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2) to hear the reference`

-- 40(2): the hearing is held in the city, town or village in which or nearest to which the appellant is ordinarily resident, unless the
-- appellant consents in writing to its being held at some other place.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 40(2) (src:326)
GIVEN `the city, town or village at which the hearing is to be held` IS A STRING
      `the city, town or village in which or nearest to which the appellant is ordinarily resident` IS A STRING
      `the appellant consents in writing to the hearing being held at some other place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40(2): the hearing of the reference may be held at that place` `the city, town or village at which the hearing is to be held` `the city, town or village in which or nearest to which the appellant is ordinarily resident` `the appellant consents in writing to the hearing being held at some other place` MEANS
        `the city, town or village at which the hearing is to be held` EQUALS `the city, town or village in which or nearest to which the appellant is ordinarily resident`
    OR  `the appellant consents in writing to the hearing being held at some other place`

-- 40(3): the Registrar notifies by registered mail the appellant, the Tribunal, the Minister and any person added as a party of the
-- date, place and time fixed.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 40(3) (src:327)
GIVEN `the date, time and place for the hearing of the reference have been fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 38: Participant in the appeal or reference`
`reg 40(3): the persons the Registrar of the Court must notify by registered mail of the date, place and time fixed for the hearing` `the date, time and place for the hearing of the reference have been fixed` `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the date, time and place for the hearing of the reference have been fixed`
    THEN append (LIST `reg 38: the appellant`, `reg 38: the Social Security Tribunal`, `reg 38: the Minister`) `any person added as a party`
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        `any person added as a party` MEANS
            IF `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` THEN LIST `reg 38: a person added as a party to the appeal` ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Procedure before Tax Court of Canada`

-- src:330 | 41 (1) Proceedings before the Court shall be informal and shall be conducted in a summary manner.
-- src:331 | (2) The judge appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2), subject to the right of all parties or their representatives to be heard, shall determine the procedure to be followed at the hearing of the reference.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 41(1) (src:330)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings before the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(1): the proceedings must be informal and conducted in a summary manner` `the proceedings are proceedings before the Court` MEANS
    `the proceedings are proceedings before the Court`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 41(2) (src:331)
GIVEN `a judge of the Court has been appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 41(2): the judge must determine the procedure to be followed at the hearing, subject to the right of all parties or their representatives to be heard` `a judge of the Court has been appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2)` MEANS
    `a judge of the Court has been appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2)`

-- 42: with the consent of the appellant the judge may require written submissions by the appellant, the Minister and any person added as a
-- party, in addition to or in place of an oral hearing.
-- src:332 | 42 The judge appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2) may, with the consent of the appellant, require that written submissions be filed by the appellant, the Minister and any person added as a party to the appeal in addition to or in lieu of an oral hearing.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 42 (src:332)
GIVEN `the appellant consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 38: Participant in the appeal or reference`
`reg 42: the persons from whom the judge may require written submissions` `the appellant consents` `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the appellant consents`
    THEN append (LIST `reg 38: the appellant`, `reg 38: the Minister`) `any person added as a party`
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        `any person added as a party` MEANS
            IF `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` THEN LIST `reg 38: a person added as a party to the appeal` ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Decision of Tax Court of Canada`

-- src:336 | 44 (1) The judge appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2) shall advise the Registrar of the Court of the judge’s decision.
-- src:337 | (2) The Registrar of the Court, after being advised of the decision in accordance with subsection (1), shall forward to the appellant, the Social Security Tribunal, the Minister and any person added as a party to the appeal a certified copy of the decision.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 44(1) (src:336)
GIVEN `the judge appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2) has reached a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 44(1): the judge must advise the Registrar of the Court of the judge's decision` `the judge appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2) has reached a decision` MEANS
    `the judge appointed pursuant to subsection 39(2) has reached a decision`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 44(2) (src:337)
GIVEN `the Registrar of the Court has been advised of the decision in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 38: Participant in the appeal or reference`
`reg 44(2): the persons to whom the Registrar of the Court must forward a certified copy of the decision` `the Registrar of the Court has been advised of the decision in accordance with subsection (1)` `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar of the Court has been advised of the decision in accordance with subsection (1)`
    THEN append (LIST `reg 38: the appellant`, `reg 38: the Social Security Tribunal`, `reg 38: the Minister`) `any person added as a party`
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        `any person added as a party` MEANS
            IF `a person has been added as a party to the appeal` THEN LIST `reg 38: a person added as a party to the appeal` ELSE EMPTY

-- src:338 | 45 No costs shall be awarded on the disposition of a reference and no fees shall be charged to the appellant by the Court.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 45 (src:338)
GIVEN `the matter is the disposition of a reference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 45: no costs may be awarded and no fees may be charged to the appellant by the Court` `the matter is the disposition of a reference` MEANS
    `the matter is the disposition of a reference`

-- src:339 | 46 If the appellant sets out a ground of appeal that has not been referred to the Court under subsection 28(2) of the Act and a ground of appeal that has been referred to the Court under that subsection, the Social Security Tribunal, on receipt of a certified copy of the decision of the Court, must proceed in accordance with the Social Security Tribunal Rules of Procedure.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 46 (src:339)
GIVEN `the appellant sets out a ground of appeal that has not been referred to the Court under subsection 28(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant sets out a ground of appeal that has been referred to the Court under subsection 28(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Social Security Tribunal has received a certified copy of the decision of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46: the Social Security Tribunal must proceed in accordance with the Social Security Tribunal Rules of Procedure` `the appellant sets out a ground of appeal that has not been referred to the Court under subsection 28(2) of the Act` `the appellant sets out a ground of appeal that has been referred to the Court under subsection 28(2) of the Act` `the Social Security Tribunal has received a certified copy of the decision of the Court` MEANS
        `the appellant sets out a ground of appeal that has not been referred to the Court under subsection 28(2) of the Act`
    AND `the appellant sets out a ground of appeal that has been referred to the Court under subsection 28(2) of the Act`
    AND `the Social Security Tribunal has received a certified copy of the decision of the Court`

